[
 {
  "id": "s01",
  "bg": "plague/bg/street.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "July fourteenth, fifteen eighteen.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 2.56,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.5,0.55,1.0,1.08,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "ft=woman@0.45,0.88,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "ft jump/laugh"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "JULY 14, 1518"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Strasbourg.",
    "start": 2.78,
    "end": 3.674,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "A woman steps into a narrow street, and starts to dance.",
    "start": 3.894,
    "end": 7.116,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "There is no music.",
    "start": 7.616,
    "end": 8.855,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_l/suspicious"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "There is no party.",
    "start": 9.075,
    "end": 10.267,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "There is no reason.",
    "start": 10.487,
    "end": 11.679,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "She does not stop for days.",
    "start": 12.179,
    "end": 13.898,
    "tags": [
     [
      "c",
      "ft arms_wide/laugh"
     ],
     [
      "a",
      "lean_in/shocked"
     ],
     [
      "s",
      "sting"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "And then her neighbours start dancing too.",
    "start": 14.118,
    "end": 16.116,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "If you are still recovering from a Halloween party last night, relax.",
    "start": 16.616,
    "end": 20.896,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "shrug/deadpan"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Whatever you did, it was not this.",
    "start": 21.116,
    "end": 23.103,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 24.203
 },
 {
  "id": "s02",
  "bg": "room",
  "layout": "host",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "Hi, I'm Archie, this is The Quiet Archive, and today's file is the strangest dance floor in history.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 7.017,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "wave/smug"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The Dancing Plague of fifteen eighteen.",
    "start": 7.237,
    "end": 9.393,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Hundreds of people.",
    "start": 9.893,
    "end": 11.082,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_up/suspicious"
     ],
     [
      "z",
      ""
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "A whole city council trying to fix it.",
    "start": 11.302,
    "end": 13.434,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "And a cure so bad it might have made everything worse.",
    "start": 13.654,
    "end": 16.653,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "So let's read the chronicles, see what actually happened, and find out why a city full of people could not stop moving.",
    "start": 17.153,
    "end": 24.234,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "hands_hips/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   }
  ],
  "duration": 25.334
 },
 {
  "id": "s03",
  "bg": "plague/bg/famine.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "First, you need to know what life in Strasbourg felt like right before this.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 4.73,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.5,0.5,1.0,1.06,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "fa=beard@0.35,0.88,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "fa think/sad"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "A VERY BAD DECADE"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The harvests had failed.",
    "start": 5.23,
    "end": 6.654,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/sad"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Bread prices shot up.",
    "start": 6.874,
    "end": 8.263,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Hail storms wrecked the crops.",
    "start": 8.483,
    "end": 10.201,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "People were genuinely starving.",
    "start": 10.421,
    "end": 12.109,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "On top of that came disease.",
    "start": 12.609,
    "end": 14.412,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_l/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Smallpox, leprosy, and a terrifying new illness called syphilis.",
    "start": 14.632,
    "end": 18.999,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "If the early fifteen hundreds had a group chat, every message would just be the skull emoji.",
    "start": 19.499,
    "end": 25.126,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "shrug/deadpan"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Keep that in mind.",
    "start": 25.626,
    "end": 26.783,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Because it is going to matter a lot later.",
    "start": 27.003,
    "end": 29.242,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 30.343
 },
 {
  "id": "s04",
  "bg": "plague/bg/street.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "Most chronicles give our first dancer a name.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 2.807,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.4,0.55,1.0,1.06,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "ft=woman@0.4,0.88,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "ft jump/laugh"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "hb=beard@0.65,0.88,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "hb facepalm/sad"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "PATIENT ZERO"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Frau Troffea.",
    "start": 3.027,
    "end": 4.071,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Mrs Troffea.",
    "start": 4.291,
    "end": 5.408,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "She danced in the street outside her home, alone, while her husband begged her to stop.",
    "start": 5.908,
    "end": 10.673,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_l/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "She kept going for days.",
    "start": 11.173,
    "end": 12.738,
    "tags": [
     [
      "c",
      "hb shrug/shocked"
     ],
     [
      "a",
      "lean_in/suspicious"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Four to six, according to one account.",
    "start": 12.958,
    "end": 15.277,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Some say a full week, only stopping to collapse and sleep.",
    "start": 15.497,
    "end": 19.248,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Eventually the authorities put her on a wagon and sent her about thirty miles away, to a shrine of Saint Vitus in a town called Saverne.",
    "start": 19.748,
    "end": 28.664,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The original patient zero.",
    "start": 29.164,
    "end": 30.825,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "shrug/deadpan"
     ],
     [
      "s",
      "boing"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "And no, not the Taylor Swift song.",
    "start": 31.045,
    "end": 32.962,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 34.062
 },
 {
  "id": "s05",
  "bg": "plague/bg/square_crowd.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "But Frau Troffea leaving did not end it.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 2.712,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.5,0.6,1.0,1.08,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "d1=woman@0.3,0.88,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "d1 jump/laugh"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "d2=sailor@0.55,0.88,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "d2 arms_wide/shocked"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "d3=beard@0.75,0.88,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "d3 jump/scared"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "30 DANCERS"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Within days, more than thirty people were dancing in the streets.",
    "start": 2.932,
    "end": 6.568,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "By August, one family chronicle says around four hundred.",
    "start": 7.068,
    "end": 10.704,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_l/shocked"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Historians argue about the numbers.",
    "start": 11.204,
    "end": 13.381,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Estimates run from about fifty to four hundred.",
    "start": 13.601,
    "end": 16.282,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "But everyone agrees on the basic picture.",
    "start": 16.502,
    "end": 18.955,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "These people did not look like they were having fun.",
    "start": 19.455,
    "end": 22.262,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "lean_in/sad"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Witnesses described blank faces, thrashing arms, swollen and bleeding feet.",
    "start": 22.482,
    "end": 27.515,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "They danced until they dropped, and then got up and danced again.",
    "start": 27.735,
    "end": 31.309,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "This was not a party.",
    "start": 31.809,
    "end": 33.23,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "think/suspicious"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "And the people of Strasbourg knew it.",
    "start": 33.45,
    "end": 35.121,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Which brings us to the city council.",
    "start": 35.341,
    "end": 37.251,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 38.351
 },
 {
  "id": "s06",
  "bg": "plague/bg/guildhall.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "The council asked the doctors.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 2.03,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.5,0.5,1.0,1.05,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "co=official@0.35,0.86,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "co point_r/smug"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "dr=writer@0.6,0.86,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "dr talk/neutral"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "THE EXPERTS"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "And the doctors had a diagnosis.",
    "start": 2.25,
    "end": 4.278,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Hot blood.",
    "start": 4.498,
    "end": 5.339,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Medical theory at the time said overheated blood could cause madness.",
    "start": 5.839,
    "end": 10.553,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_l/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The cure was not bleeding the patient.",
    "start": 10.773,
    "end": 12.752,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The cure was letting them sweat it out.",
    "start": 12.972,
    "end": 14.831,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "In other words, the medical advice for people who could not stop dancing was.",
    "start": 15.331,
    "end": 20.088,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "lean_in/suspicious"
     ],
     [
      "z",
      ""
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "More dancing.",
    "start": 20.308,
    "end": 21.255,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "I want you to sit with that for a second.",
    "start": 22.055,
    "end": 24.068,
    "tags": [
     [
      "p",
      "0.3"
     ],
     [
      "a",
      "facepalm/deadpan"
     ],
     [
      "s",
      "crickets"
     ]
    ]
   }
  ],
  "duration": 25.168
 },
 {
  "id": "s07",
  "bg": "plague/bg/stage.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "And the council went all in.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 1.813,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.5,0.55,1.0,1.06,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "mu=keeper@0.62,0.86,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "mu arms_wide/laugh"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "d1=woman@0.4,0.88,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "d1 jump/scared"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "THE WORST CURE"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The carpenters' and tanners' guild halls were turned into dance halls.",
    "start": 2.313,
    "end": 6.486,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_l/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "A wooden stage went up in the horse market, and another in the grain market.",
    "start": 6.706,
    "end": 11.027,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "They hired musicians.",
    "start": 11.527,
    "end": 12.861,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/smug"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Pipes and drums.",
    "start": 13.081,
    "end": 14.147,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "They even paid strong, healthy people to dance alongside the sick and hold them up when they got tired.",
    "start": 14.367,
    "end": 20.48,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The city basically invented the world's first viral dance challenge.",
    "start": 20.98,
    "end": 25.235,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "shrug/deadpan"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "With government funding.",
    "start": 25.455,
    "end": 26.713,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "It did not work.",
    "start": 27.213,
    "end": 28.314,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "lean_in/sad"
     ],
     [
      "s",
      "sting"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The music drew crowds.",
    "start": 28.534,
    "end": 29.936,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The crowds drew more dancers.",
    "start": 30.156,
    "end": 31.892,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "And the dancing spread faster than ever.",
    "start": 32.112,
    "end": 34.184,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 35.284
 },
 {
  "id": "s08",
  "bg": "room",
  "layout": "host",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "Now here's a question you should be asking.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 2.644,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "think/suspicious"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "WHY DID IT SPREAD?"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Why would watching people dance make you start dancing?",
    "start": 2.864,
    "end": 5.875,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The answer has a name.",
    "start": 6.375,
    "end": 7.722,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_up/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Saint Vitus.",
    "start": 7.942,
    "end": 8.809,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "People in this region believed that Saint Vitus could punish sinners by forcing them to dance.",
    "start": 9.309,
    "end": 14.801,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "A curse, basically.",
    "start": 15.021,
    "end": 16.277,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "And there had already been more than ten dancing outbreaks along the Rhine and Moselle rivers since thirteen seventy four.",
    "start": 16.497,
    "end": 23.662,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "So if you are starving, terrified, and you believe a saint might curse you into dancing.",
    "start": 24.162,
    "end": 29.511,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "lean_in/suspicious"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "And then you see your neighbour dancing.",
    "start": 29.731,
    "end": 31.512,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Uncontrollably.",
    "start": 31.732,
    "end": 32.82,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "In public.",
    "start": 33.04,
    "end": 33.872,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Your brain does not think, interesting.",
    "start": 34.372,
    "end": 36.479,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "shrug/deadpan"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Your brain thinks, oh no, it's my turn.",
    "start": 36.699,
    "end": 38.902,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "And that is not even the strangest part of this story.",
    "start": 39.402,
    "end": 42.182,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   }
  ],
  "duration": 43.282
 },
 {
  "id": "s09",
  "bg": "plague/bg/square.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "When the stages backfired, the council did a complete U turn.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 4.191,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.5,0.6,1.0,1.06,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "co=official@0.45,0.88,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "co hands_hips/angry"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "MUSIC: BANNED"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "They tore the stages down.",
    "start": 4.691,
    "end": 6.243,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_l/shocked"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "They banned public dancing.",
    "start": 6.463,
    "end": 8.005,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "They banned almost all music until the end of September.",
    "start": 8.225,
    "end": 11.511,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "There was one exception.",
    "start": 12.011,
    "end": 13.267,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/smug"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Weddings and religious celebrations could still have music.",
    "start": 13.487,
    "end": 17.19,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "But only quietly, at home, with stringed instruments.",
    "start": 17.41,
    "end": 20.592,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "No drums.",
    "start": 20.812,
    "end": 21.703,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "No tambourines.",
    "start": 21.923,
    "end": 23.103,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Fifteen eighteen.",
    "start": 23.603,
    "end": 24.77,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "shrug/deadpan"
     ],
     [
      "s",
      "boing"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The only year in history where the drummer got cancelled by the city.",
    "start": 24.99,
    "end": 29.158,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 30.258
 },
 {
  "id": "s10",
  "bg": "plague/bg/shrine.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "So they tried the other approach.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 2.1,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.5,0.5,1.0,1.06,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "pr=judge@0.7,0.86,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "pr talk/neutral"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "d1=woman@0.35,0.86,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "d1 idle/sad"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "THE RED SHOES"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Religion.",
    "start": 2.32,
    "end": 3.041,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The worst cases were loaded onto wagons and taken to the shrine of Saint Vitus at Saverne, a trip of about three days.",
    "start": 3.541,
    "end": 11.164,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_l/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "There, priests placed them under a wooden statue of the saint, gave them small crosses, and put red shoes on their feet.",
    "start": 11.664,
    "end": 18.951,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Shoes sprinkled with holy water and marked with crosses of oil.",
    "start": 19.171,
    "end": 23.171,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "And here's the thing.",
    "start": 23.671,
    "end": 24.752,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "lean_in/suspicious"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "It seems to have worked.",
    "start": 24.972,
    "end": 26.295,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Within a few weeks, the dancing faded.",
    "start": 26.515,
    "end": 28.727,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "By early September, it was over.",
    "start": 28.947,
    "end": 30.862,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Which, if it really was about fear of Saint Vitus, makes a lot of sense.",
    "start": 31.362,
    "end": 35.858,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "think/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The fear started it.",
    "start": 36.078,
    "end": 37.226,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The forgiveness ended it.",
    "start": 37.446,
    "end": 38.759,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 39.859
 },
 {
  "id": "s11",
  "bg": "plague/bg/street_night.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "Now.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 0.829,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.5,0.5,1.0,1.06,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "a",
      "idle/sad"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "HOW MANY DIED?"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The darkest claim in this story.",
    "start": 1.049,
    "end": 2.666,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "That people danced themselves to death.",
    "start": 2.886,
    "end": 4.913,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Some later accounts say that at the peak, up to fifteen people died every day.",
    "start": 5.413,
    "end": 10.289,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "That number gets repeated everywhere online.",
    "start": 10.509,
    "end": 13.127,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "But the city's own records from the time do not mention any deaths at all.",
    "start": 13.627,
    "end": 18.148,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_up/suspicious"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The big numbers come from chronicles written later.",
    "start": 18.368,
    "end": 21.004,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "So it's possible some people died of exhaustion or heart failure.",
    "start": 21.504,
    "end": 25.568,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/sad"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "But nobody knows how many.",
    "start": 25.788,
    "end": 27.422,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "And the famous figure may be exaggerated.",
    "start": 27.642,
    "end": 30.143,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 31.243
 },
 {
  "id": "s12",
  "bg": "mc/bg/study.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "About eight years later, a famous and famously arrogant doctor named Paracelsus visited Strasbourg and wrote about it.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 7.816,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.5,0.5,1.0,1.04,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "pa=writer@0.4,0.86,0.05"
     ],
     [
      "c",
      "pa point_r/smug"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "PARACELSUS"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "His diagnosis of Frau Troffea?",
    "start": 8.316,
    "end": 10.467,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_l/suspicious"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "She was not sick.",
    "start": 10.687,
    "end": 11.764,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "She was doing it on purpose.",
    "start": 11.984,
    "end": 13.7,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "To annoy her husband.",
    "start": 13.92,
    "end": 15.222,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "And the other women, he said, copied her.",
    "start": 15.722,
    "end": 17.986,
    "tags": [
     [
      "c",
      "pa arms_wide/laugh"
     ],
     [
      "a",
      "lean_in/shocked"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Also to annoy their husbands.",
    "start": 18.206,
    "end": 20.046,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Paracelsus, ladies and gentlemen.",
    "start": 20.846,
    "end": 23.1,
    "tags": [
     [
      "p",
      "0.3"
     ],
     [
      "a",
      "facepalm/deadpan"
     ],
     [
      "s",
      "crickets"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Brilliant chemist.",
    "start": 23.32,
    "end": 24.37,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Terrible marriage counsellor.",
    "start": 24.59,
    "end": 26.121,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 27.221
 },
 {
  "id": "s13",
  "bg": "plague/bg/board.png",
  "layout": "story",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "So what really happened?",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 1.659,
    "tags": [
     [
      "cam",
      "0.5,0.45,1.0,1.04,0,0"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "THEORY 1: POISON"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Modern theories.",
    "start": 1.879,
    "end": 2.94,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Theory one.",
    "start": 3.16,
    "end": 4.042,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Ergot poisoning.",
    "start": 4.262,
    "end": 5.318,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Ergot is a fungus that grows on damp rye.",
    "start": 5.818,
    "end": 8.486,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "It contains chemicals related to LSD, and it can cause hallucinations and convulsions.",
    "start": 8.707,
    "end": 14.71,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Sounds perfect.",
    "start": 15.21,
    "end": 16.257,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "shrug/deadpan"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "One problem.",
    "start": 16.477,
    "end": 17.431,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Ergot also cuts off blood flow to your arms and legs.",
    "start": 17.651,
    "end": 20.969,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "People poisoned with it could barely walk, never mind dance for days.",
    "start": 21.189,
    "end": 25.594,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Theory two.",
    "start": 26.094,
    "end": 27.016,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_up/neutral"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "THEORY 2: MASS PANIC"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The one most historians favour today, argued by historian John Waller.",
    "start": 27.236,
    "end": 31.988,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Mass psychogenic illness.",
    "start": 32.488,
    "end": 34.13,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Extreme stress, hunger and fear, plus a shared belief in a dancing curse, pushed people into a kind of trance.",
    "start": 34.35,
    "end": 41.492,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "And trances spread.",
    "start": 41.712,
    "end": 42.903,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "It sounds strange, but it has happened in modern times too.",
    "start": 43.403,
    "end": 47.047,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_l/suspicious"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "In nineteen sixty two, a laughing epidemic in Tanganyika, now Tanzania, spread through schools and villages for months.",
    "start": 47.267,
    "end": 55.746,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 56.846
 },
 {
  "id": "s14",
  "bg": "room",
  "layout": "host",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "So here's the honest version.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 2.025,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "talk/neutral"
     ],
     [
      "t",
      "DOCUMENTED vs LEGEND"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Documented.",
    "start": 2.525,
    "end": 3.463,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_up/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "In the summer of fifteen eighteen, a large number of people in Strasbourg danced uncontrollably for weeks.",
    "start": 3.683,
    "end": 10.211,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "The council built stages and hired musicians, then banned music.",
    "start": 10.431,
    "end": 14.733,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Dancers were sent to the shrine of Saint Vitus.",
    "start": 14.953,
    "end": 17.569,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "By September, it ended.",
    "start": 17.789,
    "end": 19.22,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Legend.",
    "start": 19.72,
    "end": 20.45,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "shrug/deadpan"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "That it was definitely ergot.",
    "start": 20.67,
    "end": 22.196,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "That exactly fifteen people a day died.",
    "start": 22.416,
    "end": 24.772,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "And that Frau Troffea was just trying to win an argument with her husband.",
    "start": 24.992,
    "end": 29.177,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "What it really shows is how fear can move a whole crowd.",
    "start": 29.677,
    "end": 32.772,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "lean_in/neutral"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Literally.",
    "start": 32.992,
    "end": 33.716,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "And honestly?",
    "start": 34.216,
    "end": 35.158,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "think/smug"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "A town that's starving, sick and scared, dancing because the world feels completely out of control.",
    "start": 35.378,
    "end": 41.839,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Scroll your feed today.",
    "start": 42.059,
    "end": 43.494,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "That trend never really went away.",
    "start": 43.714,
    "end": 45.741,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 46.841
 },
 {
  "id": "s15",
  "bg": "room",
  "layout": "host",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "So, your verdict.",
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 1.412,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "lean_in/suspicious"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Poison, panic, or Paracelsus was right and it was all a marriage argument?",
    "start": 1.632,
    "end": 6.808,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Tell me in the comments.",
    "start": 7.308,
    "end": 8.552,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "point_r/smug"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "I'm going with panic.",
    "start": 8.772,
    "end": 10.008,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "Mostly because I'd never survive a three day dance off.",
    "start": 10.228,
    "end": 13.856,
    "tags": []
   },
   {
    "text": "If you like true stories that history never quite finished, subscribe.",
    "start": 14.356,
    "end": 18.435,
    "tags": [
     [
      "a",
      "wave/smug"
     ],
     [
      "s",
      "ding"
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "I'm Archie, this is The Quiet Archive, and I'll see you in the next file.",
    "start": 18.655,
    "end": 23.037,
    "tags": []
   }
  ],
  "duration": 24.137
 }
]